  "solution": {
    "text": "Let, the point <math><mi>A</mi></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>B</mi></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>1</mn><mo>&gt;</mo></math><br />Required plane must be perpendicular to <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover></math><br />So, the equation of the plane is <math><mn>1</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Perpendicular distance (in units) of the point <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> from the plane is <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
